    "threads": [
      {
        "thread_id": "TH1",
        "thread_goal": "Align on MVP scope, target customers, and success metrics for the pilot.",
        "messages": [
          {
            "msg_id": "M1",
            "speaker_id": 22473,
            "reply_to": null,
            "text": "Team, kicking off our work on the new subscription product. I've put some initial thoughts in the vision doc. Please take a look and add your comments. We need to define the MVP.",
            "mentions": [
              94563,
              132848,
              242297,
              123347
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A1",
              "T1"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M2",
            "speaker_id": 94563,
            "reply_to": "M1",
            "text": "Thanks for starting this. I've reviewed A1. To help us focus, could we clarify the primary target customer segment first? The doc mentions a few possibilities. Defining this will make it easier to prioritize features and align on success metrics for T1.",
            "mentions": [
              22473
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A1",
              "T1"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "heavy_plus_sign",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M3",
            "speaker_id": 242297,
            "reply_to": "M2",
            "text": "Good point. From an operational standpoint, knowing the segment helps us anticipate the level of support they'll need. Enterprise clients have different onboarding expectations than SMBs, for example.",
            "mentions": [
              94563
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M4",
            "speaker_id": 22473,
            "reply_to": "M2",
            "text": "I was thinking we could target both to see which one works better.",
            "mentions": [
              94563
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M5",
            "speaker_id": 94563,
            "reply_to": "M4",
            "text": "Given the 30-day pilot constraint, targeting both might spread us too thin. My analysis of past product launches suggests that mid-market tech companies with an existing data warehouse but low analytics maturity are our sweet spot. They have the need, the data, and are quicker to adopt than large enterprises. This aligns with the goals for T8.",
            "mentions": [
              22473
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T8"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "bulb",
                "count": 2
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M6",
            "speaker_id": 132848,
            "reply_to": "M5",
            "text": "That sounds reasonable. We should focus on where we can get the quickest wins.",
            "mentions": [
              94563
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M7",
            "speaker_id": 22473,
            "reply_to": "M5",
            "text": "Ok, let's go with that segment then. What about features?",
            "mentions": [
              94563
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D2"
            ],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M8",
            "speaker_id": 94563,
            "reply_to": "M7",
            "text": "Great. With that segment confirmed (D2), I propose we prioritize the following for the MVP: 1) Core KPI dashboard, 2) User-level drill-down, and 3) CSV data export. We should explicitly defer features like custom alerting and API access until post-pilot. This will keep the scope tight for T2 and reduce technical risk.",
            "mentions": [
              22473
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T2"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M9",
            "speaker_id": 123347,
            "reply_to": "M8",
            "text": "From a systems perspective, that feature set is much more achievable in the timeline. Custom alerting would require significant backend work we haven't scoped.",
            "mentions": [
              94563
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "+1",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M10",
            "speaker_id": 242297,
            "reply_to": "M8",
            "text": "Agreed. A focused feature set is also easier to create support documentation and training for.",
            "mentions": [
              94563
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M11",
            "speaker_id": 22473,
            "reply_to": "M8",
            "text": "But won't customers want alerting? It seems important.",
            "mentions": [
              94563
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M12",
            "speaker_id": 94563,
            "reply_to": "M11",
            "text": "It's definitely valuable, but it's a 'delighter' rather than a core requirement for this segment's primary pain point, which is basic visibility. We can validate the core value prop first and add alerting in the next phase. This is a key mitigation for the scope creep risk mentioned in the project plan.",
            "mentions": [
              22473
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M13",
            "speaker_id": 132848,
            "reply_to": "M12",
            "text": "Deferring features is a good strategy.",
            "mentions": [
              94563
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M14",
            "speaker_id": 22473,
            "reply_to": "M12",
            "text": "Ok, I understand. Let's lock that in.",
            "mentions": [
              94563
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M15",
            "speaker_id": 94563,
            "reply_to": "M14",
            "text": "Perfect. To summarize our decisions:\n1. The primary target segment for the pilot will be mid-market tech companies. (D2)\n2. The MVP feature set is confirmed as: Core KPI dashboard, user-level drill-down, and CSV export. Custom alerting and API access are deferred. (D1)\n\nI will update A1 to reflect this and start detailing the user stories for T2.",
            "mentions": [
              22473,
              242297,
              132848,
              123347
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A1",
              "T2"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D1",
              "D2"
            ],
            "reactions": [
              {
