      {
        "thread_id": "TH3",
        "thread_goal": "Converge on pricing, subscription tiers, and discount rules.",
        "messages": [
          {
            "msg_id": "M34",
            "speaker_id": 132848,
            "reply_to": null,
            "text": "Team, here is the first look at the pricing model for T5. I've created a draft in A2 and A5. I suggest a 'Basic' and 'Pro' tier.",
            "mentions": [
              22473,
              94563,
              242297
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T5",
              "A2",
              "A5"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M35",
            "speaker_id": 22473,
            "reply_to": "M34",
            "text": "Looks like a good start. The prices seem ok.",
            "mentions": [
              132848
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M36",
            "speaker_id": 94563,
            "reply_to": "M34",
            "text": "Thanks for sharing, @132848. I have a few questions on the model in A2. The revenue assumptions seem quite aggressive for a new product. Also, the feature split between 'Basic' and 'Pro' feels a bit arbitrary. What value metric are we anchoring our pricing to? Is it users, data volume, or something else? Aligning on this will make the tiers more intuitive for customers.",
            "mentions": [
              132848
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A2"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M37",
            "speaker_id": 132848,
            "reply_to": "M36",
            "text": "I was thinking per user. It's simple. The features are just split by what seems more advanced.",
            "mentions": [
              94563
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M38",
            "speaker_id": 242297,
            "reply_to": "M37",
            "text": "From a sales and contracts perspective, per-user pricing can be complex to manage and audit. We also need very clear discount rules in A5. The current draft says 'discounts available upon request', which will create a bottleneck for approvals.",
            "mentions": [
              132848
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A5"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M39",
            "speaker_id": 94563,
            "reply_to": "M37",
            "text": "Considering our target segment, what if we explored a three-tiered approach? 'Starter', 'Growth', and 'Enterprise'. We can anchor the 'Starter' tier to the core MVP features we already defined. 'Growth' could add more advanced analytics or user seats, creating a clear upgrade path. This structure is common in B2B SaaS and easier for customers to understand. For T4, this would also allow for more nuanced financial modeling.",
            "mentions": [
              132848
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T4"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "bulb",
                "count": 2
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M40",
            "speaker_id": 22473,
            "reply_to": "M39",
            "text": "Three tiers sounds more complicated.",
            "mentions": [
              94563
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M41",
            "speaker_id": 94563,
            "reply_to": "M40",
            "text": "It can be, but it also provides more flexibility for capturing different customer segments as we grow. For the pilot, we could even decide to only offer the 'Growth' tier to keep it simple. The key is to design the structure for the future. I can mock up a strawman for the three tiers with clear feature mapping.",
            "mentions": [
              22473
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M42",
            "speaker_id": 132848,
            "reply_to": "M41",
            "text": "Ok, I can work with that. A three-tier model could work.",
            "mentions": [
              94563
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M43",
            "speaker_id": 242297,
            "reply_to": "M41",
            "text": "I support this. And for discounts, I propose we set a standard 10% that the sales team can offer, with anything up to 25% requiring manager approval. This should be documented in A5.",
            "mentions": [
              94563
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A5"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "+1",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M44",
            "speaker_id": 94563,
            "reply_to": "M43",
            "text": "That's a great, clear rule. So, let's decide. We'll move forward with a three-tier structure ('Starter', 'Growth', 'Enterprise') for the pilot, even if we only actively sell one tier initially. (D5). And we'll approve the discount thresholds: up to 10% for sales, 11-25% requires manager approval. (D6). Does everyone agree?",
            "mentions": [
              22473,
              132848,
              242297
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D5",
              "D6"
            ],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M45",
            "speaker_id": 22473,
            "reply_to": "M44",
            "text": "Yes, ok.",
            "mentions": [
              94563
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "thumbsup",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M46",
            "speaker_id": 132848,
            "reply_to": "M44",
            "text": "Agreed. I will update A2 and A5 with this new structure and the discount rules.",
            "mentions": [
              94563
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A2",
              "A5"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M47",
            "speaker_id": 242297,
            "reply_to": "M44",
            "text": "Confirmed. This is much clearer for the teams.",
            "mentions": [
              94563
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "white_check_mark",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M48",
            "speaker_id": 94563,
            "reply_to": "M46",
            "text": "Excellent. Let me know if you need a hand with the feature mapping for the tiers, happy to help.",
            "mentions": [
              132848
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M49",
            "speaker_id": 132848,
            "reply_to": "M48",
            "text": "Thanks, I might need that.",
            "mentions": [
              94563
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M50",
