      {
        "thread_id": "TH4",
        "thread_goal": "Define onboarding process and internal responsibilities for pilot customers.",
        "messages": [
          {
            "msg_id": "M51",
            "speaker_id": 242297,
            "reply_to": null,
            "text": "All, I've drafted the pilot customer onboarding process as part of T6. The draft of the A4 checklist is ready for review. I've also put together a preliminary RACI for T11 to clarify roles. Please provide your feedback.",
            "mentions": [
              22473,
              94563,
              123347
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T6",
              "A4",
              "T11"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M52",
            "speaker_id": 94563,
            "reply_to": "M51",
            "text": "This is a great, thorough start, @242297. The steps in A4 are logical. One suggestion: could we add a specific step for 'Confirm data sources and KPI alignment' right after the technical setup? This would ensure the customer sees value immediately and reduces support questions later. It also connects directly to the A7 tracker, as we can mark customers as 'fully onboarded' only after this step is complete.",
            "mentions": [
              242297
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A4",
              "A7"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "heavy_plus_sign",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
